Let a MuPDF built without its Noto and CJK fonts (MuPDF's TOFU options,
tools/build-plato.sh MUPDF_FONTS other than full) link. Plato takes the fallback
fonts for glyphs its EPUB font lacks straight from MuPDF's embedded font
symbols, which pulls in all of them (about 17 MB). build-plato.sh writes
the font set to libs/mupdf-fonts; for anything but "full", build.rs sets
cfg(mupdf_tofu), there is no fallback, and a missing glyph keeps the
font's .notdef. build.rs also reruns when the archives change, so a
rebuilt C library gets relinked.

